  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on which lottery is more left-skewed, i.e., assigns higher probability to favorable outcomes. This is directly related to what the individual considered: the higher chance of winning in A versus B. Although the term 'skewness' is not used, the individual’s attention to the probability of a favorable outcome (winning) and the dismissal of B due to its lower winning chance aligns with the core logic of the skewness-based reason. The information considered (probability of winning) matches the relevant aspect of skewness. The justification—favoring A due to much higher winning probability—corresponds to preferring the more left-skewed lottery. While the individual does not articulate the concept formally, their reasoning pattern is consistent with the decision reason. Therefore, it is highly likely the reason was used, though possibly implicitly.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
